---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Senior Tech | Aging at Home Lab" description="Plain-English guides to senior technology, medical alerts, fall detection, monitoring options, medication reminders, and caregiver apps.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Senior Tech</p>
      <h1>Technology should support care, not create more confusion.</h1>
      <p class="lede">This section will cover medical alerts, fall detection, medication reminders, privacy-safe monitoring, GPS tools, smart speakers, and caregiver apps with clear questions to ask before buying.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-grid" aria-label="Senior tech roadmap">
    <article class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-meta"><span class="badge">Roadmap</span><span class="badge warning-badge">planned</span></div>
      <h3>Medical Alert Systems: What Features Actually Matter</h3>
      <p>What to compare before choosing a pendant, watch, wall button, mobile device, or monitored system.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-meta"><span class="badge">Roadmap</span><span class="badge warning-badge">planned</span></div>
      <h3>Fall Detection Devices Explained</h3>
      <p>What automatic fall detection can and cannot do, and why families should avoid treating it as a guarantee.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-meta"><span class="badge">Roadmap</span><span class="badge warning-badge">planned</span></div>
      <h3>Cameras vs Privacy-Safe Monitoring</h3>
      <p>A practical decision guide for families comparing cameras, motion sensors, smart speakers, and check-in routines.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-meta"><span class="badge">Roadmap</span><span class="badge warning-badge">planned</span></div>
      <h3>Medication Reminder Devices</h3>
      <p>When a pill box, app, automatic dispenser, or pharmacy packaging system may be worth discussing.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="callout warning">
    <h2>Technology is not a substitute for a care plan.</h2>
    <p>Future guides in this section should avoid overpromising safety. Devices can support a plan, but they cannot eliminate risk or replace professional guidance when health, memory, mobility, or emergency concerns are present.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
